- Really?
- Yeah.

00:09:00.216 --> 00:09:01.250
- Great.
- Nice work.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.006
- Yeah I paid the price for it.

00:09:03.006 --> 00:09:04.100
- Yeah, hey what happened.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:04.933
- [Nikki] I don't know.

00:09:04.933 --> 00:09:05.766
- Thanks Phil.

00:09:05.766 --> 00:09:06.599
- Anytime.

00:09:06.599 --> 00:09:08.020
- Good luck with the rest of this wall.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:11.149
- [Phil] Yeah I don't know
what we'll do without you.

00:09:11.149 --> 00:09:11.982
(laughs)

00:09:11.982 --> 00:09:13.110
- So what do we have here?

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:15.070
So we're at The Phoenix
earthship and this is where

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.030
Mike took the concept of the earthships

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:19.680
and went wild with it and
made it really eccentric.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:22.630
And a lot of artistic
details in this building.

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:26.180
- This direction puts power to the people.

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:30.040
It empowers them to take
their energy from the sun.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.200
It's right there.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.110
It's free.

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:35.150
People should have the right
to encounter the natural

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:38.010
phenomena of this planet
to sustain themselves.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.660
- Man this is like a, like a jungle maze.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:42.090
- [Ryan] Right so this is actually where

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:43.930
the gray water starts from the sink

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:44.890
of the shower in the bathroom.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:45.960
- Do I hear birds?

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:46.793
- There's birds.

00:09:46.793 --> 00:09:47.626
- [Nikki] There's birds?

00:09:47.626 --> 00:09:48.459
- [Ryan] There's birds.

00:09:48.459 --> 00:09:50.040
Two cockatiels and two parakeets.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.260
- This is straight outta some, like

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:53.640
fantasy.
- This is Zelda level.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:54.620
- [Garrett] Is this a TV?

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:55.460
- [Ryan] Yes sir.

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:56.293
- We haven't even gone out

00:09:56.293 --> 00:09:57.660
into like the greenhouse part of it.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:58.590
- You can't argue with

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:01.000
bananas in your living room in the winter.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.300
You can't argue with the
sun heating your house.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.400
These things can be machines.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.320
So there's a long way to go.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:09.760
- [Ryan] So the house is
about 5300 square feet

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.550
and about 2000 of that
is greenhouse space.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:15.600
- There really is no limit to
what you can create out of it.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:16.433
- [Ryan] Right, and we're just scratching

00:10:16.433 --> 00:10:17.810
the surface of what's possible.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:19.670
- We're going to Puerto Rico in a month.

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:21.620
Because their power's
down, their water's down,

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.210
their infrastructure's down.

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:25.150
This building has its own infrastructure.

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:26.600
We're gonna build a building

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:29.277
that can not be blown
away by any hurricane.

00:10:29.277 --> 00:10:30.130
- [Nikki] Like living in a house

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:32.330
can be exciting and ever changing.

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:33.270
- [Garrett] It grows with you.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.950
- You take care of it
and it takes care of you.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:35.783
- Yeah.

00:10:35.783 --> 00:10:38.357
- This concept is a way
to stay alive longer.

00:10:38.357 --> 00:10:41.140
(light music)

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:44.180
- So after work today we
found that our rental car

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:46.460
had some trouble with the tires.

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:48.520
So Garrett had to drive it into town

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:50.330
and get it sorted out.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:52.420
He's not gonna be back for
another like two hours.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.300
So I started cooking dinner,

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.140
so I'm gonna pick a few sprigs,

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:57.320
aw it smells so good.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.746
I'll put that in my pasta sauce.

00:10:58.746 --> 00:11:00.030
That bowl's for Garrett when he gets done.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.650
So keep it warm for him.

00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:03.970
- Like I had to go drive
that and then drive it back.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:06.370
At the end I was just really exhausted.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:08.190
Four and a half hours later here we are.

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:09.023
- Here ya go.

00:11:09.023 --> 00:11:10.480
- Thank you Nikki.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.390
- Well there's more over
there and also there's salad.

00:11:12.390 --> 00:11:13.770
Today's been really fun,

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.860
I'm very fascinated by earthships.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:18.770
- We got to see another
earthship today which was

00:11:18.770 --> 00:11:20.860
beyond anything I could comprehend.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:23.140
Phoenix is like something
out of a sci-fi movie,

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.390
I can't imagine what it would be like

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:27.830
to complete your own earthship.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:31.340
- It's very simple in practice
but also a lot of hard work.

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:33.490
- [Nikki] That's got to be
an amazing accomplishment.

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.880
- Good morning plants.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.860
Good morning earthship.

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:43.460
Good morning.

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:44.293
- We did it.

00:11:44.293 --> 00:11:45.550
We lived in an earthship.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:48.080
It was so much more comfortable
than I thought it would be

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.630
especially since it's made out of garbage.

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:52.560
- Because this is such a
comfortable house to live in,

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.270
it's been very easy for
Garrett and I to be roommates.

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:56.974
Now the house can breathe.

00:11:56.974 --> 00:11:57.807
- Ahhhhhh

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:01.980
This is like the first time
where I'm walking away thinking

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:04.920
oh yeah I'd maybe like to
take some of these principles

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:06.550
and apply them to my own house someday.

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:09.320
- [Ryan] This is the Earthship
Village Ecologies, E.V.E.

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:11.980
This is what we're trying to
basically get an earthship

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:13.510
apartment style complex going.

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:15.420
So we have people living together.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:18.060
Working together towards
building a better future

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:19.450
as far as the homes.

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:22.400
But also growing food
together, living together

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.310
and just sharing the space and coming up

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:25.820
with a better way for the future.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:26.850
- That's kale.

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:30.010
Like I think when people
think about sustainable,

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:32.000
living that's very good for the earth,

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:35.080
they think that they have
to relinquish some comfort.

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:36.300
And we did not.

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:38.875
- The idea of building my own
earthship sounds so much fun

00:12:38.875 --> 00:12:41.740
that like maybe even when I
retire that's what I'll do.

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.120
I'll just build earthships.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:45.210
Like I can make showers that'll fit me.

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:46.900
- Everything that I've
learned here makes me

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:49.860
so excited to think
about the possibilities

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.898
of earthships and what could be next.

00:12:51.898 --> 00:12:53.340
- Bye earthship.

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:54.673
- Bye earthship.

